WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.960
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.360
A marshmallow has the shape of a cylinder

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.440
It has a diameter of 5 and a height of 3

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.380
A dessert is made with 24 marshmallows

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.220
The bottom layer consists of 3 rows of 4  marshmallows

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:23.460
The top layer consists of exact the same arrangement.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.700
Marshmallows are placed on top of the bottom layer.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.400
The dessert is completed

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:35.780
when chocolate is poured to exactly fill the gaps between the marshmallows.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.000
This is a side view of the dessert,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.340
Here's the top view of the dessert

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:48.580
Chocolate exactly fills the gaps between the marshamallows.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:51.060
The question is,

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.880
What is the volume of chocolate?

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.380
This problem was asked to grade 12 students in Australia.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:00.500
Can you figure it out?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.840
Give this problem a try, and when you're ready, keep watching the video for the solution.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.900
The main principle is that the

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:20.280
volume of the chocolate is equal to the area of the cross section of chocolate

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.260
times the height of chocolate.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.880
The dessert consists of two layers of marshmallows,

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.120
each which have a height of 3.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.580
The total height of the chocolate will therefore be 6.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:40.180
So, the volume is equal to the area of a single cross section, times 6.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.600
We can see the cross section from the top view.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.580
This forms the shape of 6 different gaps between the marshmallows.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.820
Each of the 6 gaps are identical.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:03.560
We therefore can simplify this to say that the volume is equal to 6 times the area of a single gap,

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.660
multiplied by the height of 6.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.360
So, the volume is equal to 36 times the area,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.120
of the single gap between 4 marshmallows.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:17.580
What is that area?

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:20.680
We start out

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.140
by having 4 marshmallows.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.360
Each marshmallow has a diameter of 5,

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.100
which meas the circle has a radius of 5 halves.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.200
We now draw a square that connects the center of these four circles.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.940
The square side length consists of the radius of 2 adjacent circles.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:50.020
The side length of the circle is therefore equal to the diameter of the circle.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.720
So, the side length is equal to 5.

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.600
The area between the gaps

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.440
is equal to the area of this square,

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.040
minus the area of 4 quarter circles.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.800
So we can write this as the

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.880
area of the gap is equal

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.780
to the area of the square

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:13.580
minus the area of 4 quarter circles.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.000
Now, 4 quarter circles together make one whole circle.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.880
the area of a circle is equal to 's' squared

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.760
and the area of the circle, pi r squared.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.380
This means, the area of the square is equal to

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:32.180
25, and the area of the circle is equal to 25 pi divided by 4.

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:37.400
Therefore, the area of the gap is equal to the difference between these two areas.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:42.360
We can substitute this back into our volume formula, and then simplify it

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:44.360
to get our answer that the volume is equal to

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:52.060
900 - 225 pi, which is approximately 193.1

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.560
Did you figure it out?

